WEBVTT

00:03.640 --> 00:05.320
<i>There! We're rolling.</i>

00:05.320 --> 00:09.470
<i>Today is the twins' first birthday!</i>

00:09.990 --> 00:12.180
<i>It's already been a year, huh?</i>

00:12.180 --> 00:14.610
<i>It really went by in a flash.</i>

00:14.610 --> 00:16.990
<i>You made food for me again.</i>

00:16.990 --> 00:19.550
<i>Come on! Let's eat already!</i>

00:19.550 --> 00:22.600
<i>I don't have to eat like Vash does.</i>

00:22.600 --> 00:24.520
<i>Hey, I'm a plant, too.</i>

00:25.360 --> 00:26.700
<i>This is such a waste.</i>

00:26.700 --> 00:29.470
<i>It doesn't matter whether you eat it or not.</i>

00:29.470 --> 00:32.050
<i>It's about making sure everyone gets a share.</i>

00:32.050 --> 00:33.820
<i>It's not a waste at all.</i>

00:33.820 --> 00:35.650
<i>Rem, the recording light's off.</i>

00:35.650 --> 00:36.800
<i>Oh, you're right.</i>

00:36.840 --> 00:37.320
<i>What?!</i>

00:41.010 --> 00:43.060
<i>Hey, you two!</i>

00:49.260 --> 00:51.260
You're watching that again?

00:51.260 --> 00:53.060
You're such a doting parent.

00:53.060 --> 00:55.030
Oh, you didn't know?

00:55.030 --> 00:57.340
I'm the most doting parent in the universe...

00:57.340 --> 01:00.040
of the cutest twins in the universe.

01:01.730 --> 01:04.050
Let's do a birthday party again next year.

01:04.050 --> 01:05.520
You must be joking.

01:05.520 --> 01:07.460
We will. For sure.

01:28.650 --> 01:32.190
<i>My tears scattered like bits of paper</i>

01:32.190 --> 01:35.900
<i>Scared of the unknowable tomorrow</i>

01:35.900 --> 01:39.420
<i>I lived the same day over and over,
 back and forth</i>

01:39.420 --> 01:43.250
<i>But a new morning never came</i>

01:43.250 --> 01:45.500
<i>All the reasons to calm down</i>

01:45.500 --> 01:49.930
<i>Are just some moments until the crash</i>

01:50.450 --> 01:53.430
<i>I'm no longer the one that everyone knows</i>

01:53.430 --> 01:57.730
<i>Took off the fragile armor</i>

01:57.730 --> 02:04.800
<i>I don't want to lose any more love</i>

02:05.220 --> 02:12.280
<i>I don't want to lose any more love</i>

02:12.280 --> 02:15.970
<i>There's still no line 
between today and tomorrow</i>

02:15.970 --> 02:19.540
<i>My waking nightmare doesn't end</i>

02:19.540 --> 02:23.170
<i>And yet I won't lose hope</i>

02:23.170 --> 02:29.220
<i>And yet there's no night that doesn't end</i>

02:29.220 --> 02:41.560
<i>Not here, not here</i>

02:55.820 --> 02:58.410
Nai? Where'd you go?

03:23.970 --> 03:27.010
A brilliant success! I finally did it!

03:27.800 --> 03:29.990
But you killed even <i>Rem!</i>

03:29.990 --> 03:31.520
Don't you scold me.

03:31.880 --> 03:33.740
You're my accomplice.

03:34.830 --> 03:38.530
You're the one who gave me 
the program access code!

03:47.000 --> 03:51.670
Right, Vash?

04:02.200 --> 04:05.940
I have to find Rem... Our ship...

04:19.470 --> 04:22.190
I'm sorry, I'm sorry, I'm sorry!

04:22.190 --> 04:24.570
I never imagined anything 
like this would happen!

04:46.220 --> 04:49.270
I want this all to end...

04:50.950 --> 04:53.110
I want to disappear...

04:56.550 --> 04:59.040
Hey, it's a kid! He's still alive!

05:05.670 --> 05:07.050
I knew it...

05:07.700 --> 05:10.530
There's no mistaking it. 
That's a plant reaction.

05:10.530 --> 05:12.800
He looks human to me.

05:16.420 --> 05:18.060
"Independents."

05:18.060 --> 05:20.470
Inde... whatsits?

05:20.470 --> 05:24.800
Plants are usually cloned 
from an original cell.

05:24.800 --> 05:27.870
But on rare occasion, 
plants can actually give birth.

05:27.870 --> 05:31.620
You're telling me this plant was
 born from another? Seriously?

05:33.630 --> 05:35.480
What risks does he pose?

05:35.480 --> 05:39.010
Shouldn't we toss him in a case 
like the other normal plants?

05:39.490 --> 05:41.950
No... I don't think so.

05:41.950 --> 05:45.500
You're not sure? Who knows better, then?

05:45.500 --> 05:49.700
One of the Sinners in molecular plant studies.
 Or maybe Conrad, the team leader.

05:49.700 --> 05:52.080
Conrad? From Ship Five?

05:54.750 --> 05:56.040
Where am I?

05:56.040 --> 05:57.320
Hey, he talks!

05:57.320 --> 05:59.480
Well, his genetic makeup is very human.

05:59.480 --> 06:01.050
That's not what I meant!

06:01.050 --> 06:02.910
What <i>did</i> you mean, then? You're too rattled.

06:02.910 --> 06:04.760
Ugh! Whatever.

06:04.760 --> 06:09.510
Do you remember which ship you were on?

06:10.120 --> 06:11.390
Ship Five.

06:12.610 --> 06:16.830
Do you know what happened 
to the ship? To Rem?

06:19.980 --> 06:25.100
Officer Rem Saverem, 
on duty at the time of the crash...

06:25.620 --> 06:26.720
Do you know her?

06:27.700 --> 06:30.490
She raised us.

06:30.490 --> 06:31.530
"Us"?

06:31.530 --> 06:34.310
Were there other Independents?

06:35.240 --> 06:39.350
Just one more... But he's probably dead.

06:39.350 --> 06:43.080
So you ditched everyone and ran on your own?

06:43.080 --> 06:44.130
What a shit.

06:44.680 --> 06:46.190
Come on, Brad!

06:47.630 --> 06:49.450
He's hiding something.

06:49.450 --> 06:52.350
You think he's suspicious? He's just a kid.

06:52.350 --> 06:54.260
I'll go find Ship Five.

06:54.260 --> 06:57.180
It's been over eighty hours since the crash.

06:57.180 --> 06:59.890
There's very little chance anyone survived.

06:59.890 --> 07:04.440
Maybe they activated their gravity plant
 in the nick of time like we did.

07:08.440 --> 07:10.490
Why did you save me?

07:10.490 --> 07:11.200
Huh?

07:11.730 --> 07:13.820
I wanted to die there.

07:14.900 --> 07:18.270
We're only here because we got lucky.

07:18.270 --> 07:22.220
So we survivors can't talk like that,
 even if we don't mean it.

07:29.120 --> 07:31.810
Let's think about what 
we can do starting now.

07:37.470 --> 07:38.640
What's your name?

07:39.060 --> 07:40.390
Vash.

07:40.390 --> 07:42.890
I'm Luida Leitner.

07:42.890 --> 07:46.870
I wound up in charge of this ship, Ship Three.

07:48.020 --> 07:49.860
Can I ask you a few questions?

07:50.710 --> 07:54.370
What do you produce as a generator?

07:54.370 --> 07:58.030
Electricity? Chemical compounds? 
Or maybe amino acids?

07:58.030 --> 07:59.190
Nothing.

07:59.890 --> 08:03.250
Unlike normal plants, I can't make anything.

08:03.710 --> 08:09.810
The other one wasn't like me.
All I do is eat, drink, and sleep.

08:09.810 --> 08:12.960
Right. Like a human.

08:13.840 --> 08:17.970
You told me to think about
 what I can do starting now...

08:17.970 --> 08:21.360
But I can't do anything. Nothing at all.

08:35.750 --> 08:38.660
Brad called in.

08:38.660 --> 08:43.120
He rescued survivors from Ship Five, 
but Rem wasn't there.

08:43.620 --> 08:48.060
The ship was in ruins, 
so I'm sorry. She probably...

08:52.190 --> 08:56.870
Rem stayed aboard until the bitter end,
 trying to stop the crash.

08:56.870 --> 08:58.920
The survivors told us.

09:04.600 --> 09:07.100
This is all you could find of Rem's?

09:07.100 --> 09:10.510
We spent two weeks in the rubble to find this.

09:10.510 --> 09:12.520
I don't want to hear any complaints.

09:12.520 --> 09:15.400
I'm sorry. Did you find anything else?

09:15.400 --> 09:17.370
We recovered the black box.

09:17.370 --> 09:21.580
It's badly damaged, though.
Not sure if we can analyze it.

09:21.580 --> 09:26.120
There's also this, but it's no good.

09:26.630 --> 09:31.060
Ship Five was destroyed, 
and ours is in pretty bad shape...

09:31.060 --> 09:32.970
We're stuck.

09:32.970 --> 09:36.430
So, how long are you going
 to keep that kid around?

09:38.390 --> 09:40.100
Didn't like the food?

09:40.540 --> 09:44.200
I'm not going to eat it. 
You should stop bringing it to me.

09:44.200 --> 09:45.390
It's a waste.

09:46.750 --> 09:50.020
It doesn't matter whether you eat it or not.

09:52.920 --> 09:55.360
We found this in the ruins of Ship Five.

09:58.920 --> 10:00.990
She really cared for you.

10:02.800 --> 10:07.900
Believe in yourself. There has to be 
something that only you can do.

10:12.410 --> 10:15.450
I can't do anything...

10:15.930 --> 10:18.550
Is that the monster?

10:18.550 --> 10:20.290
Look at him! So grotesque.

10:20.290 --> 10:21.970
Just kill him already.

10:28.550 --> 10:32.560
Meeting you has brought me so much joy...

11:11.070 --> 11:13.530
There's no point keeping him alive.

11:13.530 --> 11:16.620
Like he said, he's a plant 
that doesn't produce anything.

11:16.620 --> 11:18.760
Luida, are you listening?

11:18.760 --> 11:21.950
Hold on. I'm almost done reconstructing this.

11:22.300 --> 11:23.280
Got it!

11:24.220 --> 11:26.500
<i>Critical error in navigation settings.</i>

11:26.500 --> 11:28.520
<i>Time to emergency cryosleep recovery is...</i>

11:28.520 --> 11:32.040
<i>One hour?! They won't make it
in time at this rate...</i>

11:32.040 --> 11:36.390
<i>The injection data was replaced?! 
Who did this...?</i>

11:32.750 --> 11:34.250
Wait, is this...

11:36.390 --> 11:41.950
<i>Manually repairing trajectory control system. 
Control thrusters at maximum.</i>

11:41.950 --> 11:43.050
<i>Please hurry!</i>

11:43.690 --> 11:44.980
It's the electricity plant!

11:47.970 --> 11:50.640
The flower... is opening up?

11:52.370 --> 11:55.110
What is this? 
Its vitals are all over the place.

11:55.110 --> 11:56.340
What's causing it?

11:56.340 --> 11:57.570
I don't know.

11:58.260 --> 12:03.170
If, let's say, the plants aren't compatible 
with this planet's environment...

12:03.170 --> 12:05.620
We all die out here?

12:06.830 --> 12:09.250
After all we've been through to survive...

12:09.250 --> 12:10.810
Isn't there anything we can do?

12:12.070 --> 12:14.020
Hey! Come to the cell!

12:16.920 --> 12:18.010
What's wrong?

12:18.010 --> 12:19.420
It's the kid!

12:21.360 --> 12:23.760
Hey! Did something happen to the plant?!

12:24.770 --> 12:25.970
How did you know?

12:25.970 --> 12:27.960
Must have overheard it somehow.

12:28.500 --> 12:31.980
I'm sorry, but we're busy. 
I have to get back there...

12:31.980 --> 12:33.740
Its voice! I can hear it!

12:33.740 --> 12:36.180
The plant is calling out for help!

12:36.180 --> 12:38.770
Don't trust him. 
He's just making stuff up to get out.

12:38.770 --> 12:42.230
Let me meet the plant! 
Its voice is fading!

12:42.860 --> 12:44.550
He's gotta be lying!

12:45.320 --> 12:47.960
At this rate, the plant...

12:49.220 --> 12:50.310
Luida.

12:52.010 --> 12:54.930
You heard the reconstruction earlier, right?

12:54.930 --> 12:55.810
Huh?

12:55.810 --> 12:57.630
I don't know who Rem was, but...

12:57.630 --> 12:58.960
Whoa, whoa.

12:58.960 --> 13:03.010
She sacrificed herself trying 
to stop that great crash.

13:03.010 --> 13:05.140
I'm sure it's safe.

13:05.140 --> 13:06.120
Hey!

13:06.120 --> 13:08.350
Rem trusted him. I do, too!

13:19.250 --> 13:22.610
<i>Do you remember that story I told you before?</i>

13:23.100 --> 13:27.610
<i>We all have a blank ticket 
with no listed destination.</i>

13:27.610 --> 13:30.910
<i>What you put there is up to you.</i>

13:31.510 --> 13:33.630
<i>No matter the darkness you find yourself in,</i>

13:33.630 --> 13:38.540
<i>you'll always have that ticket 
waiting for you to write in where to go.</i>

13:38.870 --> 13:44.010
<i>Nai, Vash... The two of you will be just fine.</i>

13:51.820 --> 13:55.110
I can hear you. Don't worry.

14:10.990 --> 14:13.310
I'm right here.

14:23.460 --> 14:27.050
Thank you, Vash. 
You saved a lot of lives today.

14:27.050 --> 14:30.710
It was nothing. I just did what I could.

14:38.120 --> 14:39.220
Come with me.

14:45.730 --> 14:46.860
What's this?

14:46.860 --> 14:48.540
Your room!

14:48.540 --> 14:52.580
Starting today, you're officially 
a resident of Ship Three.

14:53.150 --> 14:57.160
I'm sorry for how we treated you before now.

15:04.920 --> 15:06.420
Thank you, Luida!

15:06.420 --> 15:11.660
Thank Brad, too. I wouldn't have been 
able to convince everyone on my own.

15:11.660 --> 15:12.890
Brad?

15:12.890 --> 15:14.920
Hey, I told you not to tell him.

15:15.430 --> 15:17.250
He's nicer than he looks.

15:19.170 --> 15:22.010
Instead of handcuffs, 
you'll have a guard from now on.

15:22.010 --> 15:23.510
Bear with us for a little while.

15:23.510 --> 15:25.750
We won't need that before long either.

15:25.750 --> 15:29.200
Who knows? I still don't trust him.

15:29.200 --> 15:31.520
One wrong move, 
and I'll let you have it.

15:31.520 --> 15:32.790
Sure, sure.

15:33.820 --> 15:38.580
Oh, and Vash, about what we do starting now...

15:39.680 --> 15:42.790
Could you take a look 
at the other plants as well?

16:29.840 --> 16:31.720
Are you tired?

16:31.720 --> 16:32.760
Yeah.

16:32.760 --> 16:35.410
This is our fifth trip this year.

16:35.410 --> 16:38.220
Thanks for coming along, Brad.

16:38.220 --> 16:43.020
Like I said, my mission's 
just to keep an eye on you.

16:44.070 --> 16:47.980
Besides, this is heaven compared 
to how things were after the crash.

16:54.780 --> 16:57.520
Have a drink. It's a long ways back.

17:00.370 --> 17:01.970
You're a nice guy, Brad.

17:02.490 --> 17:03.660
Though you look scary.

17:03.660 --> 17:04.470
Give that back.

17:04.470 --> 17:05.960
No way!

17:05.960 --> 17:07.310
You little...

17:07.310 --> 17:08.330
Jeez.

17:11.190 --> 17:12.200
Vash.

17:13.220 --> 17:14.010
What's up?

17:17.430 --> 17:18.960
Ta-da!

17:18.960 --> 17:22.430
This is for you, Vash! 
It's from everyone on Ship Three.

17:22.430 --> 17:27.430
Wow, it's brand new! 
Clothes are so hard to get.

17:30.270 --> 17:32.470
What a pretty shade of red.

17:32.470 --> 17:34.050
Is it too flashy?

17:34.050 --> 17:38.110
No, I like red. Rem did, too.

17:38.110 --> 17:40.950
She raised lots of red geraniums.

17:40.950 --> 17:42.460
Geraniums?

17:42.460 --> 17:43.080
Yeah.

17:44.730 --> 17:48.160
Thank you. I'm so glad 
I get to live with you all.

17:48.160 --> 17:49.910
This is my home.

17:49.910 --> 17:53.630
Your home, huh? I love that!

17:53.630 --> 17:58.140
I've been thinking for a while now 
 that "Ship Three" is a little bland.

17:58.140 --> 18:01.180
Starting today, we'll call this place home!

18:03.350 --> 18:06.040
Yours and ours.

18:13.820 --> 18:15.730
This is still a bit big for me.

18:17.450 --> 18:19.460
Home, huh...

18:25.460 --> 18:28.990
You're getting along with Vash
 better than I thought.

18:28.990 --> 18:33.310
Not really. I'm just making sure 
he doesn't do anything bad.

18:33.310 --> 18:35.230
You just can't be honest.

18:36.060 --> 18:40.470
That's... the black box. 
I thought you couldn't repair it.

18:40.470 --> 18:44.480
Not back then. But it's been 
five years. Things change.

18:44.480 --> 18:46.320
The tech, my skills...

18:46.780 --> 18:49.110
Lots of people are still blaming themselves

18:49.110 --> 18:52.120
because we don't know what caused the crash.

18:55.510 --> 18:56.580
I did it!

19:00.360 --> 19:02.320
Hey, is that...

19:04.570 --> 19:07.330
<i>A brilliant success! I finally did it!</i>

19:07.330 --> 19:09.470
<i>But you killed even </i>Rem!<i></i>

19:10.060 --> 19:12.040
<i>Don't you scold me.</i>

19:12.040 --> 19:14.070
<i>You're my accomplice.</i>

19:14.950 --> 19:18.340
<i>You're the one who gave me 
the program access code.</i>

19:18.340 --> 19:20.460
Who's that with Vash?

19:20.460 --> 19:24.900
It has to be the other Independent.
He didn't die in the crash after all.

19:24.900 --> 19:26.490
Why would he lie about that?

19:26.490 --> 19:28.850
Because they're working together, that's why!

19:28.850 --> 19:33.020
He's never been on the side of us humans!

19:33.480 --> 19:35.980
He's been betraying us this whole time!

19:52.260 --> 19:54.290
He heard us.

19:54.290 --> 19:58.210
There has to be a clue here 
about the other Independent.

20:06.590 --> 20:07.610
Find something?

20:11.460 --> 20:16.710
<i>Thanks to everyone, I was able to 
get back on my feet again.</i>

20:17.580 --> 20:20.760
<i>I consider all of you as family,</i>

20:21.820 --> 20:25.120
<i>so I couldn't continue to lie.</i>

20:25.870 --> 20:27.120
<i>I'm so sorry.</i>

20:29.120 --> 20:33.110
<i>No matter how much you want to 
forget the past, there is no escape.</i>

20:34.330 --> 20:36.890
<i>It's time for me to face</i>

20:38.380 --> 20:42.760
<i>that an Independent will make up 
for what an Independent did.</i>

20:43.510 --> 20:46.440
"This is my atonement."

20:47.660 --> 20:49.140
We have to go after him.

20:49.850 --> 20:50.830
Don't stop me.

20:50.830 --> 20:52.360
I won't.

20:52.360 --> 20:56.150
When you see Vash, please apologize 
for me. I said some terrible things.

20:58.260 --> 21:01.780
Tell him yourself. I'm bringing him back!

21:32.860 --> 21:34.100
Home...

21:35.540 --> 21:37.500
Did they save me?

22:16.660 --> 22:17.840
Nai...

22:20.020 --> 22:27.640
<i>Your light...</i>

22:34.100 --> 22:38.400
<i>If that light never changes</i>

22:38.400 --> 22:42.830
<i>And continues to shine high above the sky</i>

22:42.830 --> 22:47.140
<i>Even when I'm lost, 
even when I'm struggling</i>

22:47.140 --> 22:51.390
<i>I'll continue to search for you</i>

22:51.390 --> 22:55.680
<i>Even on days of sickness or sadness</i>

22:55.680 --> 23:00.060
<i>I'll open the window to a new morning</i>

23:00.060 --> 23:04.250
<i>I'm moving forward, I'm standing still</i>

23:04.250 --> 23:07.810
<i>Tell the people who are praying</i>

23:07.810 --> 23:13.770
<i>But today this flower 
before me is praising you</i>

23:13.770 --> 23:16.780
<i>My song is a song of joy and wishes</i>

23:16.780 --> 23:19.500
<i>Yes, I'm reaching out</i>

23:19.500 --> 23:24.840
<i>But you're too high up 
in the evening stars</i>

23:24.840 --> 23:30.810
<i>But today this flower 
before me is praising you</i>

23:30.810 --> 23:33.960
<i>My song is a song of joy and wishes</i>

23:33.960 --> 23:36.660
<i>Yes, I try to reach out</i>

23:36.660 --> 23:41.820
<i>But you're too high up 
in the evening stars</i>
